--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Bundled third-party data
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The source of this crate holds third-party data: the colormaps the renderer
offers, the color names an imported color table may use, and the names of the
WMO's originating centers and sub-centers. It is redistributed under its own
terms:

  * This product includes color specifications and designs developed by Cynthia
    Brewer (https://colorbrewer.org/). The red–blue and brown–teal diverging
    maps are from ColorBrewer, © Cynthia Brewer, Mark Harrower and The
    Pennsylvania State University, licensed under the Apache License, Version
    2.0.
  * The turbo colormap is © 2019 Google LLC (Anton Mikhailov), licensed under
    the Apache License, Version 2.0.
  * Viridis, plasma and cividis are from matplotlib and are released into the
    public domain (CC0) by their authors: Nathaniel J. Smith, Stéfan van der
    Walt and Eric Firing (viridis, plasma), and Jamie R. Nuñez, Christopher R.
    Anderton and Ryan S. Renslow (cividis).
  * The cool–warm diverging map is Kenneth Moreland's Smooth Cool Warm, which
    was first featured in ParaView and is covered by ParaView's BSD license,
    © 2000 Kitware Inc. That license is below.
  * The color names an imported color table may use are the X11 color database
    (`rgb.txt` from X.Org `app/rgb`), © 1985, 1989, 1998 The Open Group, used
    under the X11 permission notice in that repository's `COPYING`.
  * The GRIB2 parameter, surface and time-range names, and the names of
    originating centers, sub-centers and chemical constituents, are generated
    from the World Meteorological Organization's code tables
    (https://github.com/wmo-im/GRIB2 and https://github.com/wmo-im/CCT),
    published under the MIT License. Their LICENSE.md is below.

The grayscale colormap is a plain black-to-white ramp made here.

